Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt76x02: rearm MAC work after channel changes

mt76_set_channel() cancels the PHY's MAC work before invoking the
driver's channel callback. The mt76x0 and mt76x2 callbacks do not
requeue it. This leaves the periodic MAC error check, TX status
timeout sweep and statistics updates inactive after the first
channel change.

Requeue the work in the three channel callbacks, covering mt76x0
PCI/USB and mt76x2 PCI/USB. Also requeue it if the mt76x2 USB
channel command fails, as the callback resumes the MAC in that
case as well.

Fixes: f4fdd7716290 ("wifi: mt76: partially move channel change code to core")
Assisted-by: LLM

---
diff --git a/mt76x0/main.c b/mt76x0/main.c
--- a/mt76x0/main.c
+++ b/mt76x0/main.c
@@ -26,6 +26,9 @@
 		tasklet_enable(&dev->dfs_pd.dfs_tasklet);
 	}
 	mt76x02_pre_tbtt_enable(dev, true);
+
+	ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev), &dev->mphy.mac_work,
+				     MT_MAC_WORK_INTERVAL);
 
 	return 0;
 }
diff --git a/mt76x2/pci_main.c b/mt76x2/pci_main.c
--- a/mt76x2/pci_main.c
+++ b/mt76x2/pci_main.c
@@ -49,6 +49,9 @@
 
 	tasklet_enable(&dev->dfs_pd.dfs_tasklet);
 	tasklet_enable(&dev->mt76.pre_tbtt_tasklet);
+
+	ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev), &dev->mphy.mac_work,
+				     MT_MAC_WORK_INTERVAL);
 
 	return 0;
 }
diff --git a/mt76x2/usb_main.c b/mt76x2/usb_main.c
--- a/mt76x2/usb_main.c
+++ b/mt76x2/usb_main.c
@@ -45,6 +45,9 @@
 	mt76x2_mac_resume(dev);
 
 	mt76x02_pre_tbtt_enable(dev, true);
+
+	ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev), &dev->mphy.mac_work,
+				     MT_MAC_WORK_INTERVAL);
 
 	return err;
 }
